From: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Updates for OE cross builds

A cross build has no network during configure, and a distribution wants
one copy of each library, so take every dependency from the platform
instead of fetching a private copy.

- get_cmake_cuda_archs.py checked platform.machine(), the build host,
  so cross builds for Thor from x86_64 got no CUDA architecture. Use
  the target machine.
- Align requests with what the layers ship: cccl, nanobind, googletest
  and MatX by version; spdlog and GoogleTest through find_package
  (GoogleTest GLOBAL, as holoscan_add_dependency() scopes imported
  targets away from the test directories); iceoryx2 by probing for the
  publisher callbacks HoloMQ needs.
- Fetch yyjson and reflect-cpp only when no provider target is
  declared. With a declared provider, config_io, its tests and the
  parameter web tuner link the library instead of compiling its
  sources, and leave yyjson_api alone so its symbols stay visible.
- Guard install rules that only apply to a fetched copy: flatbuffers on
  Flatbuffers_ADDED, bundled CV-CUDA on HOLOSCAN_VISION_BUNDLE_CVCUDA
  (new, default ON), the dataset download scripts on
  HOLOSCAN_INSTALL_DATA_DOWNLOAD_SCRIPTS (new, default ON).
- Exempt imported yaml-cpp from the static archive check: config_io
  links it PRIVATE behind $<BUILD_INTERFACE:>, so it is never exported.
- In the installed package, keep the normal package root for fmt,
  dlpack and FlatBuffers when the provider was found rather than
  fetched, since the private root holds only fetched copies, and find
  CCCL when no fetched CCCL recorded it.
- HOLOSCAN_USE_CUDA_TOOLKIT_NVTX (new, default OFF) maps nvtx3 to
  CUDA::nvtx3 instead of fetching NVTX, since no toolkit ships an nvtx3
  package.
- Move the example source behind the existing
  HOLOSCAN_INSTALL_EXAMPLE_SOURCE, but keep the test driver scripts and
  the holomq_main and plan_artifacts_workspace_test binaries, so the
  installed tree can replay the example ctests.
- Install each benchmark binary beside its source under
  share/benchmark, and move the benchmark source behind
  HOLOSCAN_INSTALL_BENCHMARK_SOURCE (new, default ON).
- Add NOSTRIP to nanobind_add_module: nanobind links release builds
  with -Wl,-s, leaving nothing to split into -dbg.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific]
Signed-off-by: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
